WEBVTT

00:09:56.676 --> 00:10:00.236
with nature and technology
working hand in hand

00:10:00.236 --> 00:10:02.676
to take CO2 out of the sky

00:10:02.676 --> 00:10:03.676
and keep it out.

00:10:05.116 --> 00:10:07.276
Which brings me neatly back ...

00:10:07.276 --> 00:10:08.556
to the woolly pigs.

00:10:08.836 --> 00:10:09.836
(Laughter)

00:10:10.476 --> 00:10:13.636
Now, these woolly pigs live
on an estate on the Isle of Mull,

00:10:13.636 --> 00:10:16.276
which is owned by Jim Mann’s
Future Forest Company.

00:10:17.676 --> 00:10:20.196
And I know they don’t look very dangerous,

00:10:20.196 --> 00:10:22.316
but they are actually
the closest you can get

00:10:22.316 --> 00:10:24.516
to a native Scottish wild boar

00:10:24.516 --> 00:10:26.916
without having to have
a dangerous animals license.

00:10:27.236 --> 00:10:31.116
And they do what the Scottish
wild boars used to do.